# Local prompt-engineering harness for Claude Code / Codex prompts — dev
# tooling, not part of the published project. See .agent-harness/README.md.
/.agent-harness/

# Local working notes. HANDOFF.md is the in-flight branch's status note
# (see AGENTS.md). RELEASE-PLAN.md is a guard rather than a pointer to an
# existing file — release process lives in RELEASING.md and nowhere else.
/HANDOFF.md
/RELEASE-PLAN.md

# Ad-hoc before/after review captures. Unlike docs/screenshots/native-baseline
# (written by scripts/capture-brand-assets.js) and docs/screenshots/refinement,
# these are one-off comparison dumps from a review pass: nothing in the build,
# the docs, or a script reads them, so they are local evidence rather than
# project assets.
/docs/screenshots/consolidation/
/docs/screenshots/native-baseline-consistency/

# Ad-hoc manual QA scratch files (e.g. reproducing a reported bug's exact
# markup to eyeball in a real browser) — local only, not the published
# examples gallery (see docs/examples.md, tracked separately under gh#29).
/examples/

# Duplicate files left beside real ones as "name 2.png", "name 3.png" —
# Eleventy would publish them as pages and Playwright would collect them as
# specs, so they are ignored rather than tolerated.
#
# This used to say iCloud Drive was the cause. It is not: the repository is
# not under a File Provider root, no file carries the `dataless` flag, and
# `fileproviderctl` lists no provider covering this path. What does create
# them is still unidentified — tracked as gh#102, which also holds the
# count and the cleanup decision.
#
# Note the breadth: this also ignores any legitimate file whose name
# contains a space followed by a digit ("Figure 1.svg"). Nothing in the
# project is named that way today; check here first if a file you added
# silently fails to appear in `git status`.
* [0-9]*
